From 2ab7ae424a12ce4c6b61b800f1cea089cfaa783a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 21:45:55 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(drilling): state the through-hole break-through and
 say where it goes

Through holes ran a hidden, fixed 1.0 mm (a pitch for a thread) past
the part bottom. Drill, Bore and Thread now carry `break_through`
(mm, `None` = the kind's old figure, so every existing op posts
byte-identical and keeps its digest): a Break-through field in the
hole kinds' Levels group, `break_through` in the project file
(project v63, written only when stated) and the MCP params JSON.
Generation notes the run and the deepest tip in the document unit;
a tip under the stock bottom with no workholding modelled is named
(`Break-through below stock:`), and one that reaches modelled steel
is refused by the fixture law (a flute hit holds the post). A
negative value is refused at creation; a lathe's axial or cross
drill refuses a stated value by name.

Fixes #1557

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX
